.TH HEE 1 "2026-09-06" "HEE" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hee \- Human Execution Engine command dispatcher
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hee
[\fBhelp\fR | \fBlist\fR]
.br
.B hee
\fIsubcommand\fR [\fIargs...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hee
is a thin dispatcher. It is the checkout, not an installed toolchain:
\fB~/.local/bin/hee\fR is a symlink to
\fB~/git/human-execution-engine/tooling/bin/hee\fR, and every subcommand is an
executable next to it. Pulling the repo is the update mechanism; there is no
second copy to drift.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
Built-in:
.TP
.B help
Show help. Works after any verb, and nothing to the right of it is executed.
.TP
.B list
List every available subcommand, built-in and extension.
.TP
.B lint
Validate HEE object envelopes.
.TP
.B "hooks install"
Install this repo's git hooks.
.TP
.B "git merge"
Mass review/approve/merge open PRs.
.TP
.B "ssh send-keys"
Distribute SSH keys between hosts.
.TP
.B "contract review"
Review contract objects.
.SH EXTENSIONS
Any executable named
.I hee\-<cmd>
in the target repo's
.I tooling/bin
or the tool repo's, resolved in that order \(em so
.B hee check
runs
.IR tooling/bin/hee\-check .
Run
.B hee list
for the current set; it is derived from what is present, not from a list
kept here.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.local/bin/hee
The dispatcher on PATH; a symlink into the checkout below.
.TP
.B ~/git/human-execution-engine/
The checkout. \fItooling/bin/\fR holds every subcommand; \fItooling/heerc\fR is
sourced by \fI~/.bashrc\fR and sets PATH and per-oper preferences.
.TP
.B ~/.hee/index/_.yaml
This oper's SOA anchor (hee-soa.v1): host, user, machine id, stool hash. Read
by \fBhee ver session\fR for a human shell's signature tag.
.TP
.B ~/.hee/current/
Per-oper working state (the SOA legs and hashes the anchor refers to).
.TP
.B ~/.hee/bin/
Only present once \fBhee tools-update\fR has installed a pinned external tool
there. Not the dispatcher, not the subcommands.
.SH COMPLETION
None is installed by anything yet. A generated bash completion file is tracked
as human-execution-engine#564.
